4.2 UNIFYING CURVATURES VIA EDGENET
The key distinction of GNRF from other GNNs lies in its ability to perceive time-varying edge curvature. However, curvature is often computationally expensive. For instance, calculating the resistance curvature κRC requires computing the matrix pseudo-inverse, while Ollivier-Ricci curvature
